1	CR Details
1.1	Description
Following feature is to be developed as part of Fincore Phase 3. Multifactor implementation
1.2	Scope of Changes
FinCore application to implement second factor authentication, by sending One Time Passcode (OTP) to users registered mobile number and/or email address.
1.3	Executive Summary
Login into FinCore application to be allowed using multiple authentications, by adding additional layer of OTP verification to strengthen account security, without breaking the current LDAP authentication mechanism.






2	Solution
2.1	Technical Feasibility of the Proposed Solution
The solution proposed in this document is technically feasible subject to assumptions and limitations. 
2.2	Scope of changes
Currently on entering the valid User ID and password user is allowed to access the FinCore application. With this change upon submitting the valid credentials application will send the One Time Passcode. To implement the OTP verification in FinCore application following changes are in scope. 
•	Mobile/Email Check
•	Code generation
•	Code sending
•	Resending
•	Wrong Attempts
•	Expiry
•	Verification
OTP will be compulsory for every user trying to login in the FinCore application. The login screen shall undergo changes in order to accommodate this functionality.
2.2.1	Mobile/Email Check
Upon valid credentials entered by the user, application to check if mobile number and/or email address present in database. If neither is present code shall not be sent.
2.2.2	Code generation
Application to generate 6-digit random code when user id has either mobile number or email id. The code to be hashed using bcrypt before storing and not in plain text.
2.2.3	Code Input
After sending the code, the application shall display the input for 6-digit code and await user input for validation. Only numeric inputs to be allowed.
2.2.4	Code Sending
The code to be sent to both the registered mobile number and email id or whichever is present. Application shall show masked mobile and/or email to which code has been sent.
2.2.5	Resending
Application to enable resend button after 60 seconds. A maximum of 3 resends shall be allowed per user within a 10-minute window. Every resend to regenerate a new code and reset the attempt counter.
2.2.6	Wrong Attempts
Every generated code to have 5 attempts for verification. Upon entering a wrong code for 5 times, it will be marked as expired and user need to click on resend code button for receiving a new code.
2.2.7	Code Expiry
An OTP to be considered as Expired under either of the following conditions:
1.	After 5 minutes from the time of its generation
2.	5 consecutive failed verification attempts
User can’t login with the expired code. 
2.2.8	Verification
Upon successful verification of the code user is allowed to use the application. The validated code to be immediately invalidated and deleted to ensure that it is for one-time use only.
2.2.9	OTP entry Screen time-out
In case the user remains idle on OTP entry screen for 15 minutes, the user will be prompted to enter user ID and password again.
